Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): order the delivery line by readiness, not by
 number alone (J3)

The ai.ubq.fi delivery line ordered every active contender with a clean
latest review by pull request number, and held every record behind any
contender in flight on the tip. Contenders that could not deliver therefore
held it ahead of green, reviewed heads whose rounds were spent: red heads
returned to work for their CI fix (629, 610, 615, 617), heads awaiting their
CI before a review on a moved base (605, 662, 597, 602, 1128, 1130) and, at
01:25Z, CI-fixed legacy heads refreshed onto the tip awaiting their CI before
their final review (672, 673, 693, 694, 754), which refresh again on every
tip move and so never leave. 698 (PR 1112) and 879 (PR 1120), and behind the
same holders 605 (PR 1054), 597 (PR 1089) and 602 (PR 1092), deferred for
hours with nothing written.

Each contender now has a standing against the tip (`lineStanding`): landing
(a carried refresh in flight, reviewed on the tip waiting to merge, a carried
refreshed head on the tip), ready (deliverable now on a moved base: spent,
latest review clean, its next step the mechanical refresh), re-review
(heading for a review round on the tip), reviewed (a round left, in delivery
on a moved base) or waiting (not deliverable now). A spent record waits only
behind a landing contender or a ready one with a lower number, so it takes
the line as soon as it is deliverable; a record with a round left also waits
behind every ready one, a re-review and a lower reviewed one, as before. One
record lands at a time, so the launcher's one merge per pass moves the base
once. The carried step that reads a spent reviewed head green clears a stale
`ci_pending` wait once before it defers, so the line sees it ready; later
deferrals write nothing.

Runtime only (src/repair); the launcher's imports from the line
(`holdsDeliveryLine`, `lineBefore`) are unchanged. No new state shape,
blocker, wait or stdout line: the one new write is a `wait: null` at
`delivery`, a shape R80 writes itself, and R80's own line holds every other
record behind a refresh this line admitted (tested against R80's source when
its commit is present).

Tests: live replays of the 20:36Z and 01:25Z states (verbatim records,
tests/fixtures/repair/delivery-line-live.json), every standing, and a
ten-record fleet through the real loop and the real launcher delivery pass:
one merge on every pass from the second, deliverable heads in pull request
order, a head that turns green taking its place ahead of every higher number.

